/-! Phase 2 keystone: deployed-row S-box reconstruction for the
`gadget.state_commitment_path` slice (9015 rows, 24 quad-path rounds).

The deployed slice flattens each Poseidon4 (width-5) S-box into a five-row chain
`square,square,square,square,mul` (see `…GadgetStateCommitmentPath9015_193a70`
`step0..step4`). This file proves that exact five-row chain collapses to the
closed `Poseidon4Bridge.p17 = x^17`, reusing the canonical rate-4 round/perm
specs (`fr5`/`pr5`/`permSpec4`) the abstract bridge already builds on.

This is the reusable unit for the per-round reconstruction; the remaining Phase 2
work composes it across the 24 rounds + MDS mix into `QuadPath24.circuit` and
applies `AnchorMerkle.concrete_circuit_sound24`. -/

namespace Shieldd.GnarkFormal.Deployed.StateCommitmentPath

open Shieldd.GnarkFormal.Poseidon4Bridge
open Shieldd.GnarkFormal.Extracted.PoseidonHash4 (F Order)

variable [Fact (Nat.Prime Order)]

/-- A deployed five-row S-box chain (`x²; x⁴; x⁸; x¹⁶; x¹⁶·x`) reconstructs the
closed `p17 x = x^17`. Width-agnostic; one instance per S-box across all 24
rounds. Mirrors the proven `Deployed.NoteCommitment.p17_from_rows`. -/
theorem p17_from_rows (x v0 v1 v2 v3 v4 : F)
    (h0 : x * x = v0) (h1 : v0 * v0 = v1) (h2 : v1 * v1 = v2)
    (h3 : v2 * v2 = v3) (h4 : v3 * x = v4) :
    v4 = p17 x := by
  unfold p17
  rw [← h4, ← h3, ← h2, ← h1, ← h0]


/-- Full Poseidon4 round from deployed rows: once the five S-box outputs are
pinned to `p17` of their constant-offset inputs (via `p17_from_rows`), the round
